1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:06,370
Here's a timeline we built of ancient
Egypt: from its first farming cultures,

2
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:10,800
through the unification under
Narmer around three thousand BCE,

3
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:14,900
to the death of Cleopatra
in 30 BCE. Periods,

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:18,850
dynasties and the reigns of
major pharaohs are bands;

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,450
monuments, battles and writings are moments,
each linked to the article it draws

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,559
on.

7
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:30,049
Ancient dates are estimates, and
scholars' chronologies differ,

8
00:00:30,099 --> 00:00:33,329
so this timeline follows
one standard chronology,

9
00:00:33,379 --> 00:00:37,329
the Oxford History of
Ancient Egypt, and says so.

10
00:00:37,379 --> 00:00:42,549
Where Egypt split, the bands
show it. Around 1650 BCE,

11
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:47,559
the Hyksos kings rule the north from
Avaris while Theban kings hold the south,

12
00:00:47,609 --> 00:00:50,280
until Ahmose drives the Hyksos out.

13
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:55,970
Zoom into the Old Kingdom.
Djoser's Step Pyramid,

14
00:00:56,020 --> 00:01:01,060
the first great building in stone.
Sneferu's pyramids at Dahshur,

15
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:06,850
where the true pyramid shape was worked
out. Then Khufu's Great Pyramid at Giza,

16
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,630
and the Sphinx, usually credited to
Khafra: all in a little over a century,

17
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:14,220
each linked to the king who built it.

18
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:21,330
Open a moment to read it. The Diary of
Merer: the logbook of a crew shipping

19
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:26,290
limestone to Giza, the oldest
inscribed papyrus known.

20
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:30,720
And its date says how sure it is: from
about Khufu's twenty-seventh year,

21
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:34,360
later than his reign
ends in this chronology.

22
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:37,650
Every early date here is
an estimate, and says so.

23
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:44,000
A thousand years later, in the
New Kingdom, two reigns overlap.

24
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:47,240
Hatshepsut rules as king
beside her young stepson,

25
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:51,560
Thutmose the Third, and sends
ships to Punt. After her,

26
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:55,760
he wins at Megiddo and builds
an empire; late in his reign,

27
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:58,759
her images are cut from her monuments.

28
00:02:00,189 --> 00:02:05,809
Ramesses the Second reigns sixty-six
years. Open the Battle of Kadesh,

29
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:09,239
against the Hittites:
it's linked to his reign,

30
00:02:09,289 --> 00:02:13,359
and to the peace treaty fifteen years
later, whose text survives from both

31
00:02:13,409 --> 00:02:17,218
sides. Follow the link and keep reading.

32
00:02:18,948 --> 00:02:22,528
How do we know any of
this? Separate by tags,

33
00:02:22,578 --> 00:02:26,578
choose writing, and the record
rises into a track of its own:

34
00:02:26,628 --> 00:02:29,318
the first labels at Abydos,
the Narmer Palette,

35
00:02:29,368 --> 00:02:33,488
the Palermo Stone's annals, the
Pyramid Texts, the Story of Sinuhe,

36
00:02:33,538 --> 00:02:37,998
letters and treaties, and Manetho,
the priest whose thirty dynasties

37
00:02:38,048 --> 00:02:40,421
Egyptologists still count by.

38
00:02:42,071 --> 00:02:45,301
The Rosetta Stone's decree
is dated to the day:

39
00:02:45,351 --> 00:02:51,941
the twenty-seventh of March, 196 BCE.
Historical dates keep it as the sources

40
00:02:51,991 --> 00:02:56,384
give it, in the Julian calendar,
beside the timeline's own.

41
00:02:58,114 --> 00:03:03,094
Cleopatra the Seventh comes
to the throne in 51 BCE.

42
00:03:03,144 --> 00:03:07,614
Caesar, Antony, Actium.
In August of 30 BCE,

43
00:03:07,664 --> 00:03:12,174
Alexandria falls, and within
two weeks she is dead.

44
00:03:12,224 --> 00:03:14,656
Egypt becomes a Roman province.

45
00:03:16,286 --> 00:03:22,166
Now keep going, on the same scale.
Cleopatra lived closer in time to the Moon

46
00:03:22,216 --> 00:03:25,205
landing than to the building
of the Great Pyramid.

47
00:03:28,206 --> 00:03:32,806
Anyone can read it, no account
needed. Build one with your class,

48
00:03:32,856 --> 00:03:34,766
and share it with a link.
